# Tutorial 01 — the start screen, the interface and the Cedar House sample.
title: Getting started
summary: The start screen, the interface tour and the Cedar House sample
---
open start
caption "Welcome to Oanarina Archi Tool" "A free, native Mac app for drafting and building design"
wait 3
note "Start an empty drawing, open a project or build the sample house" at start "New Drawing" for 4
wait 3.5
caption "Sample projects" "The Cedar House: the house this tutorial series builds step by step"
hover start "Cedar House"
wait 1.5
click start "Cedar House"
wait 2.5
caption "The ribbon" "Tools grouped in tabs; every button runs a command you could also type"
note "Home, Insert, Annotate, Architecture, View, Output…" at tab Architecture for 3.5
click tab Architecture
wait 2
hover ribbon WALL
wait 1.5
hover ribbon DOOR
wait 1
click tab Home
wait 1
caption "The canvas" "The 2D plan of the current level: scroll to zoom, drag to pan"
move 10500,6000
wait 1
zoom window -500,0 11500,10500
wait 1.5
zoom extents
wait 1
caption "The command line" "Just start typing: commands, options and coordinates"
note "Prompts and [options] appear here" at commandline for 3.5
type ZOOM E
wait 1.5
caption "Side panels" "Properties, Layers, Levels, project Browser, Materials and more"
click panel Layers
wait 2
click panel Levels
wait 2
click panel Properties
pick 3000,1500
wait 2.5
note "The selected wall's type, material, height and thickness" at panel Properties for 3
wait 3
escape
caption "The status bar" "Snaps, grid, ortho and polar tracking toggles, cursor coordinates"
note "Click to toggle, or press F3, F7, F8, F10…" at status OSNAP for 3.5
hover status ORTHO
wait 1.2
hover status OSNAP
wait 2.5
caption "2D, 3D, Split and Sheet" "Switch the workspace with these buttons or ⌥⌘1–4"
click mode 3D
wait 2.5
orbit 50 4
wait 1
camera Corner
wait 2.5
click mode Split
wait 3
click mode Sheet
wait 2.5
click mode 2D
caption "Next: the command line" "Tutorial 02 shows how to drive the app by typing"
wait 3
